--- !u!114 &612804565
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 612804563}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: acb1ed5b80d48ee4b9f75a375fe20f84, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DayakattamDungeon.UI.InteractiveTutorialDialog
  titleText: {fileID: 1527463400}
  categoryBadgeText: {fileID: 458733397}
  pageIndicatorText: {fileID: 862080618}
  illustrationImage: {fileID: 1454556635}
  imagePlaceholderText: {fileID: 1654735896}
  descriptionText: {fileID: 332733024}
  bulletsText: {fileID: 624046755}
  tipText: {fileID: 1270842957}
  prevButton: {fileID: 1294333644}
  nextButton: {fileID: 397122408}
  closeButton: {fileID: 1218186036}
  dotsContainer: {fileID: 551107177}
  dotPrefab: {fileID: 0}
  slides:
  - title: The Sacred Tamil Dice Duel
    category: 'STEP 1: HERITAGE & GOAL'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    description: 'Dayakattam (Thayam) is an ancient tactical board game played across
      Tamil Nadu for millennia during auspicious festive gatherings.


      Four
      players sit at the corners of a sacred 7x7 board. Your goal is to guide all
      3 Kalasam spirit pawns clockwise around the outer loop, spiral through the
      inner rings, and ascend into the Central Sacred Palace.'
    bulletPoints: "\u2022 <b>Objective:</b> First player with all 3 pawns in the
      Palace wins.\n\u2022 <b>Match Size:</b> 2-Player (You vs Grandma) or 4-Player
      (You, Mama, Grandma, Dada).\n\u2022 <b>Spiritual Theme:</b> Awaken spirit pawns
      from your altar into the sacred mandala."
    tip: You must enter through your own colored threshold (South Red) before spiraling
      inward!
  - title: Rolling The Brass Dayakattam
    category: 'STEP 2: DICE & LUCKY NUMBERS'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    description: 'Dayakattam is played with two oblong brass stick dice with numbered
      long faces: 0, 1, 2, and 3.


      The dice sum gives your movement value
      (1 to 6). But if both sticks land on blank (0 + 0), that roll triggers the
      fabled <b>12 (Pannirendu)!</b>'
    bulletPoints: "\u2022 <b>Auspicious Rolls (1, 5, 6, 12):</b> Grants an immediate
      <b>+1 Extra Roll</b>!\n\u2022 <b>Combo Multiplier:</b> Chaining lucky rolls
      powers up your combo (1x \u2192 1.5x \u2192 2x \u2192 3x).\n\u2022 <b>Ending
      Rolls (2, 3, 4):</b> Standard rolls end your rolling turn and begin the Action
      Phase."
    tip: Bank multiple rolls during a lucky streak, then spend them strategically
      across your pawns!
  - title: Awakening & Board Movement
    category: 'STEP 3: THAYAM & ACTION PHASE'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    description: Your pawns begin resting in your team's sanctuary tray. Before a
      pawn can step foot onto the board, it must be awakened by the sacred number
      <b>1 (Thayam)</b>.
    bulletPoints: "\u2022 <b>Awakening:</b> Spend a banked roll of <b>1</b> to place
      a pawn onto your colored Entry tile.\n\u2022 <b>Movement:</b> Click a banked
      roll, then click any active pawn (or drag it) to move clockwise along its spiral
      route.\n\u2022 <b>Flexible Spending:</b> You can spend different banked rolls
      on different pawns in any order."
    tip: Rolling Thayam (1) gives an extra roll AND lets you enter a new pawn simultaneously!
  - title: Sanctuary Tiles & Combat Cuts
    category: 'STEP 4: TACTICS & CUTTING'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    description: The board has 8 crossed <b>Sanctuary</b> tiles (the 4 entry midpoints
      + 4 inner corners). These tiles grant divine immunity from opponent strikes.
    bulletPoints: "\u2022 <b>Sanctuary Immunity:</b> Pawns on crossed tiles can co-exist
      safely without being captured.\n\u2022 <b>Striking / Cutting:</b> Landing exactly
      on an opponent pawn on an uncrossed tile cuts them back to their reserve!\n\u2022
      <b>Cutting Bonus:</b> Successfully cutting an opponent pawn awards a massive
      Auspicious Multiplier boost."
    tip: Always prioritize parking vulnerable pawns on crossed Sanctuary tiles when
      ending your turn!
  - title: Ascension Into The Palace
    category: 'STEP 5: VICTORY & ADVANCEMENT'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    description: After completing the outer perimeter loop, your pawns turn inward
      into the concentric middle and inner rings, spiraling toward the Central Palace.
    bulletPoints: "\u2022 <b>Inner Spiral:</b> Follow your illuminated trail to navigate
      inward.\n\u2022 <b>Palace Goal:</b> Reaching the center requires an exact or
      valid entrance count.\n\u2022 <b>Victory & Unlocks:</b> Defeat Grandma in 2-Player
      mode to unlock the chaos of 4-Player Mode with Mama and Dada!"
    tip: Click '? Rules & Lore' at any time to reopen this guide, or press 'Interactive
      Tutorial' on the Title Screen!
